<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Morat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1476">1476</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Murten · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundian-wars">Burgundian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Morat was fought on 22 June 1476 at Murten, west of Bern, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundian-wars">Burgundian Wars</a>. The Swiss Confederates relieved the town, held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adrian-von-bubenberg">Adrian von Bubenberg</a> against a siege by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, and routed his army with heavy losses. With his defeat at Grandson earlier that year, it broke Burgundian power and led to Charles's death at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a> in 1477.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-morat.jpg" alt="Battle of Morat" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diebold Schilling der Ältere · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schilling_murten.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Zürich contingents fought alongside the other cantons in the Burgundian Wars, with Hans Waldmann commanding Zürich’s troops at the <b>Battle of Morat</b> in 1476, and in the Italian Wars until the defeat at Marignano in 1515.</blockquote><a href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Canton of Zürich · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…the Bold created standing companies of ordinance in 1471 and a powerful artillery train, but his army was routed by the Swiss Confederates at the Battle of Grandson and the <b>Battle of Morat</b> in 1476, and he was killed at the Battle of Nancy on 5 January 1477.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Duchy of Burgundy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Burgundian Wars they defeated Charles the Bold of Burgundy at the Battle of Grandson and the <b>Battle of Murten</b> in 1476 and, as allies of Duke René II of Lorraine, at the Battle of Nancy in 1477, where Charles was killed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Old Swiss Confederacy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>It led the Swiss against Burgundy, with Adrian von Bubenberg holding <b>Murten</b> in 1476.</blockquote><a href="/state/canton-of-bern">Canton of Bern</a></li></ul></section>
